  "source_type": "database",
  "citation": "FooDB v2020-04-07 (Wishart DS et al., foodb.ca). Content sources: USDA.",
  "doi": "",
  "url": "https://foodb.ca/downloads",
  "notes": "Organic components mapped from FooDB compounds to BiGG via InChIKey/name. Mineral base added. Bounds presence-based; foodb_content retained. Unmapped measured compounds kept in uncovered (v2 completeness fix). IMPORTANT: composition values are taken from the archived FooDB 2020-04-07 CSV data release; FooDB's live food page no longer displays this bulk composition, so it will appear empty. Verify individual compounds via the per-component cross-reference links. Underlying content was aggregated by FooDB from USDA / DTU / Phenol Explorer.",
  "data_release": "FooDB 2020-04-07 CSV release (foodb.ca/downloads)",
  "food_record": "https://foodb.ca/foods/FOOD00786",
  "verification": "expert-curated (multi-source food composition; growth-relevant profile completed, FooDB noise removed)",
  "curation_date": "2026-07-17",
  "curation_sources": [],
  "curation_notes": "Cane (blackstrap-type) molasses. Dominant carbon/energy sources: sucrose (~29 g/100g) plus invert sugars glucose+fructose (~25 g/100g), with organic acids lactic (~4.8 g/100g) and aconitic (~1.1 g/100g) as major secondary substrates that were entirely missing from the FooDB record. High mineral load (K, Mg, Ca) and B-vitamins (B6, B5, B3). Amino-acid and organic-acid amounts are converted from % dry matter (~78% DM) of peer-reviewed cane-molasses datasets; USDA FDC 168820 supplies the sugar/mine",
  "curation_added": [
   "aconitic acid (cane-signature organic acid, ~1.1 g/100g)",
   "lactic acid (~4.8 g/100g, dominant organic acid)",
   "citric acid",
   "malic acid",
   "acetic acid (minor organic acids)",
   "aspartic acid",
   "glutamic acid",
   "alanine",
   "valine",
   "leucine",
   "GABA (free amino acids)",
   "betaine (nitrogenous osmolyte)",
   "crude protein / amino-N total",
   "biotin (B7)",
   "sulfate and chloride amounts",
   "quantitative amounts for sucrose, glucose, fructose and all minerals/vitamins"
  ],
